      "text": "imports         = ast, json, re, subprocess, sys, Path, jedi\n\nPROMPT          = the ask text for one block: sequent rules, root rules, body rules, two gold bodies\nVOCAB           = the ask text for the vocabulary pass: shared terms plus rewritten texts\nRULES           = each rule name with one plain line that defines it\nBLOCK_RULES     = the rule names every block carries\nCALLS           = a one-cell counter of claude calls\nTRIES           = the number of tries one block answer gets\nNAME_REF        = the pattern for a lone name in parentheses\nDOTTED          = the pattern for a dotted name\n\nask_claude      = one claude -p run, the JSON pulled out of the answer    (ask_claude)\ncheck_block     = the gate on one block answer: sequent, root, real links, bang marks    (check_block)\ncheck_grounded  = the gate on term meanings: real block names, no circle of terms    (check_grounded)\ncheck_vocab     = the gate on the vocabulary answer: terms, rewritten texts, term use    (check_vocab)\ncarve           = the free line spans of a range, minus the used spans, blanks trimmed    (carve)\nblocks_of       = one block per def and class plus the script block, with carved lines    (blocks_of)\ncalls_of        = the block names one block calls, found in its syntax tree    (calls_of)\nlayers_of       = a height per block, so a block sits above the blocks it calls    (layers_of)\nlinks           = the name links jedi finds between blocks    (links)\ncompile_block   = one block explained: ask, check, retry up to 4 times    (compile_block)\nvocab_pass      = all texts rewritten through a shared vocabulary, up to 4 tries    (vocab_pass)\nmain            = the whole run: cut, order, explain bottom up, compress, write map.json    (main)\n\nentry point     = run main() when the file starts as a script    (script)",
