      "text": "label     = the block's name for the prompt: its short name plus (), or \"the top-level script code\"\nspan      = the block's line ranges as one text, like \"338-359\"\nshort     = the short names of all blocks, the list the prompt shows as legal link names\nbase      = the PROMPT text filled in: file name, numbered code, label, span, the ctx note, short\nnote      = extra repair text that grows after a failed try, empty at first\nerrs      = the list of rules the answers broke so far\n\nup to 4 tries:\n    m     = claude's answer to base plus note, pulled out as JSON    (ask_claude)\n    rec   = the answer checked against the rules    (check_block)\n                the sequent: takes, gives, effects - what the block needs, returns, and does to the world\n                the root: the one answer line, 15 words or less\n                the links: the answer can name a block in parentheses, like (carve) - each such name must be a real block of this file\n                the bang marks: an effect is what a block does to the world - it writes a file, prints a line, runs a program\n                               a step line that performs an effect starts with \"! \", and the \"! \" lines and the effects list must agree\n    a good answer: print one status line, return rec - the loop ends here\n    a broken answer: print the retry, add the error to errs\n    note  = the last answer, the rule it broke, and every rule broken so far, so the next try repairs it\n\nafter 4 broken tries: stop the whole program with an error    (sys.exit)",
